WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.559 --> 00:00:07.579
over a decade – so now that it's all&nbsp;
over, what was it all really about?

00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:12.859
The final episodes of The Walking Dead&nbsp;
put the ensemble cast at center stage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:19.039
Characters continue to grow and develop. Eugene&nbsp;
and Max expose Sebastian and his mother Pamela's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:23.899
disdain for the people of the Commonwealth.&nbsp;
Yumiko shuns respectability to stand by her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.899 --> 00:00:28.879
friend. And Daryl steps into the position of&nbsp;
father figure for Judith. At the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.879 --> 00:00:35.179
Father Gabriel rediscovers his faith after taking&nbsp;
an almost sadistic turn earlier in the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.179 --> 00:00:38.599
while Connie and Kelly speak&nbsp;
truth to power at every turn.

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:44.179
The Commonwealth was always going to be a&nbsp;
deconstruction of class politics rearing their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:48.979
ugly head even as the zombie apocalypse&nbsp;
raged. But the series found a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:53.659
deliver a message of solidarity, resistance,&nbsp;
and power to the people in its final episode.

00:00:54.679 --> 00:01:00.259
Another major theme of Season 11 was standing&nbsp;
by your family no matter what and the way that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:06.079
loyalty creates a feeling of home — even for a&nbsp;
crew being attacked from all sides. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.079 --> 00:01:11.839
Daryl and Leah originally bond over their&nbsp;
shared isolation, with Leah holed up in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.839 --> 00:01:16.879
cabin in the woods that Daryl stumbles upon&nbsp;
in his solo travels. Leah is a tragic figure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.879 --> 00:01:21.333
a loner looking for a community while&nbsp;
Daryl stands with his found family.

00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:25.939
"I would've died for Carl. You know that."

00:01:25.939 --> 00:01:30.799
He and Leah are opposite sides of a coin.&nbsp;
Leah chooses to follow a corrupt leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:36.199
which is a pattern Daryl also fell into during&nbsp;
his early appearances. Now, with people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.199 --> 00:01:41.359
care about him, he's able to make things right.&nbsp;
Leah, however, lacks that support and is lost.

00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:48.439
Similarly, Negan is one of the series' scariest&nbsp;
villains, having killed both Abraham and Glenn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:54.019
while very nearly breaking Rick in the process.&nbsp;
After spending a lot of time – much of it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.019 --> 00:01:58.939
prison – with the people of Alexandria, he's&nbsp;
still convinced he's an eternal outsider. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:04.039
after finding love and family with Annie, Negan&nbsp;
seems like a new man. He's even able to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:08.959
amends to some of the people he hurt, back&nbsp;
when he was a big bad. He admits to Ezekiel,

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:13.339
"You're all better than me, and&nbsp;
if you think I don't know that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.255
then you haven't been paying attention."

00:02:18.619 --> 00:02:24.079
Invasion of the Commonwealth by a zombie horde&nbsp;
inevitably means losing some long-time fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.079 --> 00:02:28.999
favorites. That includes Luke, who we meet in&nbsp;
the 9th season as part of Magna's crew. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:34.219
the comics see Luke dying during the war with the&nbsp;
Whisperers, he avoids that fate in the TV series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:39.799
Luke leaves for Oceanside with his girlfriend&nbsp;
Jules in the 10th season. Along the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.799 --> 00:02:45.979
they run into Aaron, Lydia, Jerry, and Elijah,&nbsp;
who advise them to avoid Oceanside at all costs.

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:47.599
"It's gone, man."

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.039
"What do you mean, gone?"

00:02:49.039 --> 00:02:50.179
"It ain't ours anymore."

00:02:50.899 --> 00:02:56.539
Luke is reunited with his former traveling&nbsp;
companions, but the reunion is tragically brief.

00:02:56.539 --> 00:03:01.459
When the walls of the Commonwealth are breached,&nbsp;
Luke has to be torn away from Jules as she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:06.739
devoured before his eyes. He, too, sustains&nbsp;
major injuries and perishes in the struggle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:10.999
despite his friends' attempts to save him. After&nbsp;
realizing that there's nothing they can do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.999 --> 00:03:15.919
they say goodbye. Yumiko pulls out Luke's&nbsp;
harmonica and presses it into his hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.919 --> 00:03:20.179
telling him that he always brought music&nbsp;
to their lives. This is a major callback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.179 --> 00:03:24.079
to their early appearances on the show,&nbsp;
and makes it clear how much they've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.079 --> 00:03:27.603
through and grown to depend on&nbsp;
each other, even when far apart.

00:03:28.363 --> 00:03:33.559
Watching Daryl evolve from a young man whose&nbsp;
loyalties are divided between his toxic brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.559 --> 00:03:39.379
Merle and Rick's crew into the gruff but tender&nbsp;
lone wolf he becomes is one of the great delights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:44.539
of The Walking Dead. Daryl may prefer to work in&nbsp;
solitude, but he's developed a sense of community&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.539 --> 00:03:50.239
and family over the years that was impossible&nbsp;
to foresee early on. With Rick and Michonne out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:55.399
of the picture, Season 11 sees him stepping&nbsp;
more into a father figure role for Judith.

00:03:55.399 --> 00:04:00.859
"There's one thing I know. There's a whole bunch&nbsp;
of people back there, they'd do anything for you."

00:04:01.559 --> 00:04:06.559
Even as Daryl attempts to protect Judith, she&nbsp;
makes it clear that she has no intention of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.559 --> 00:04:10.699
sitting on the sidelines and insists on&nbsp;
being included in the journey back into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.699 --> 00:04:15.559
the Commonwealth. Daryl reluctantly agrees to&nbsp;
let her come along but regrets it immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.559 --> 00:04:19.939
when they are ambushed and Judith is shot&nbsp;
by Pamela. Though Judith pulls through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.939 --> 00:04:24.559
it's only through a transfusion of Daryl's&nbsp;
blood. In what could be a throwaway line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.559 --> 00:04:27.499
Daryl mentions that he knows&nbsp;
he's a universal donor.

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:32.889
"Mine goes with anybody. Merle used to make&nbsp;
me sell it when I was a kid, for money."

00:04:32.889 --> 00:04:37.639
This makes his gentleness and care toward&nbsp;
Judith all the more touching as we remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:42.033
the world of confusion and pain Daryl&nbsp;
has endured to find his real family.

00:04:42.135 --> 00:04:43.275
"Daryl?"

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.328
"Yeah."

00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:47.239
"You deserve a happy ending, too."

00:04:47.239 --> 00:04:48.079
Rosita's sacrifice

00:04:48.079 --> 00:04:52.699
Rosita started as a supporting character&nbsp;
and evolved into a woman able to hold her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:57.259
own with series stalwarts like Michonne or&nbsp;
Daryl. When we meet her in the 4th season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.259 --> 00:05:01.009
she's involved in a deteriorating&nbsp;
relationship with Abraham –

00:05:01.009 --> 00:05:05.030
"If you're lost, please just tell me. The gas&nbsp;
in this tank is worth more than your ego."

00:05:05.686 --> 00:05:07.519
– which then turns to jealousy as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.519 --> 00:05:12.559
he moves on with Sasha. Later, she has a&nbsp;
brief affair with Siddiq, followed by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.559 --> 00:05:16.819
surprisingly healthy relationship with Father&nbsp;
Gabriel, with whom she raises a daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.819 --> 00:05:22.279
Coco. It's her commitment to being a good mother&nbsp;
that defines her adventures in the last season as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.279 --> 00:05:28.039
she becomes a full-fledged action hero, starring&nbsp;
in some top-notch zombie melees along the way.

00:05:28.039 --> 00:05:30.379
Rosita's end is devastating.

00:05:30.533 --> 00:05:35.513
"Dammit, Eugene. Go. I'm right behind you."

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:41.839
Her heroism and willingness to put everyone ahead&nbsp;
of herself sees her bitten and slowly transforming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.839 --> 00:05:47.419
throughout the final episode. Still, this season&nbsp;
was a boon to Rosita fans. She stepped up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.419 --> 00:05:52.519
Daryl to defend the Commonwealth, never mincing&nbsp;
words about where her true loyalties lie. When we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.519 --> 00:05:58.519
first met Rosita, Eugene had an unrequited crush&nbsp;
that took seasons to resolve. But in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.519 --> 00:06:03.259
he's the one who stays with her. He's the&nbsp;
last face she sees, cementing their status&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.259 --> 00:06:07.940
as one of the most endearing and genuine&nbsp;
friendships this side of Carol and Daryl.

00:06:08.479 --> 00:06:13.879
The final episode of Season 11 has to move fast&nbsp;
to fit in everything set up in earlier episodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.879 --> 00:06:19.879
One of the most vital arcs is that of Mercer. A&nbsp;
loyal soldier of the Commonwealth, he appears at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:24.919
first to be humorless and unflappable until we&nbsp;
see Princess' unique charm loosen him up a bit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.919 --> 00:06:30.319
Mercer's loyalties are in question throughout&nbsp;
the season. His duty to the people is in direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:35.179
conflict with his love for his sister, Max,&nbsp;
who becomes a public enemy after revealing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.179 --> 00:06:39.319
Sebastian and Pamela's callous attitudes&nbsp;
toward the people they're meant to serve.

00:06:39.319 --> 00:06:43.579
Yet, Mercer turns around in the end&nbsp;
and proves that there are positives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:48.079
to standing by one's convictions. Rather&nbsp;
than becoming a tool of a fascist state,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.079 --> 00:06:53.359
he shifts loyalties and takes the troops with him.&nbsp;
When it comes time to hold Pamela accountable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.359 --> 00:06:58.219
he's at the front of the group. And when she&nbsp;
calls him a traitor, he turns the tables on her.

00:06:58.394 --> 00:07:06.854
"You disappeared hundreds of citizens. Led&nbsp;
the dead to our doorstep. You shot a child."

00:07:07.399 --> 00:07:12.619
The central drive behind Season 11 is the&nbsp;
importance of placing faith in people rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.619 --> 00:07:16.999
than institutions or politicians, and&nbsp;
nowhere is that arc better embodied than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.999 --> 00:07:22.187
through Mercer — a man who refuses to live&nbsp;
life following orders he knows are unjust.

00:07:22.993 --> 00:07:27.739
No character in "The Walking Dead" has had&nbsp;
it particularly easy, but Aaron and Lydia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.739 --> 00:07:32.299
have truly gone through the wringer. Aaron&nbsp;
lost both his husband Eric and his lover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.299 --> 00:07:38.239
Jesus. He saw his wish for a better future for&nbsp;
Alexandria dashed through Lance Hornsby's lies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.239 --> 00:07:43.759
Season 11 has him experiencing his own dark&nbsp;
side only to turn things around through his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.759 --> 00:07:48.919
mentorship of Lydia. Likewise traumatized&nbsp;
by her years as a pawn in Alpha's game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.919 --> 00:07:53.899
surrounded by death and hate, Lydia is in&nbsp;
desperate need of support and family when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.899 --> 00:07:57.859
she comes to the Commonwealth, and Aaron&nbsp;
is one of the primary people to offer it.

00:07:57.859 --> 00:08:02.359
Perhaps more than anyone, Aaron has&nbsp;
always been able to put hope and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.359 --> 00:08:04.699
desire to serve his friends&nbsp;
and family at the forefront,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.699 --> 00:08:08.833
and that selflessness has played a major&nbsp;
role in his relationship with Lydia.

00:08:09.069 --> 00:08:13.329
"Loss is inevitable. It always has been."

00:08:13.329 --> 00:08:18.259
He encourages her to take every moment&nbsp;
of joy she can find with Elijah. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.259 --> 00:08:22.100
he coaxes her through the loss of her&nbsp;
arm while reflecting on his own loss.

00:08:22.362 --> 00:08:27.402
"You'll feel it sometimes. Like it's still there."

00:08:27.794 --> 00:08:31.514
Recognizing his own hope and&nbsp;
pain in Lydia, he reassures her,

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:39.379
The Walking Dead examines what makes a true&nbsp;
leader. Rick occasionally slides into rhetoric,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.379 --> 00:08:44.359
which is directly challenged by Michonne when&nbsp;
he's at the end of his rope. While Negan commands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.359 --> 00:08:49.939
total loyalty in those he leads, his ruthlessness&nbsp;
makes him vulnerable. People have genuine faith in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.939 --> 00:08:54.859
Rick's ability to show mercy, and ultimately&nbsp;
turn to him over Negan. Again and again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.859 --> 00:09:00.259
those who gain power through cruelty are knocked&nbsp;
back down. It's an optimistic view of humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.259 --> 00:09:04.039
despite the violence of villains&nbsp;
like Pope, the Governor, and Alpha.

00:09:04.039 --> 00:09:09.919
King Ezekiel loses his realm to the Saviors,&nbsp;
but he remains a man of the people regardless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.919 --> 00:09:14.539
of what occurs. Always willing to step in&nbsp;
and help wherever he is needed — be it as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.539 --> 00:09:19.399
a decision-maker or a helper — Ezekiel has&nbsp;
proven himself to be a true leader time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.399 --> 00:09:24.379
again by never letting his ego get the better&nbsp;
of him. When the going gets tough, he leads a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.379 --> 00:09:29.239
group of prisoners to shield Negan with their&nbsp;
bodies despite their shared animosity. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.239 --> 00:09:34.339
the kind of selfless act that makes him co-leader&nbsp;
of the post-Milton Commonwealth alongside Mercer.

00:09:34.999 --> 00:09:40.699
The final episode of the 10th season, "Here's&nbsp;
Negan," presents a full-focus flashback of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.699 --> 00:09:45.739
Negan's life before he became the terrifying&nbsp;
leader of the Saviors. Though this was meant to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.739 --> 00:09:51.379
flesh out Negan's backstory and give some context&nbsp;
for atrocities to come, the episode occurs in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.379 --> 00:09:56.299
context of Maggie's return to Alexandria, as&nbsp;
she presents an immediate threat to his life.

00:09:56.299 --> 00:10:02.299
"If you stay here, she will kill you. I just&nbsp;
didn't want your death on my conscience."

00:10:02.899 --> 00:10:07.579
One of Negan's greatest crimes is the murder&nbsp;
of Abraham and Glenn in front of their friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.579 --> 00:10:12.799
which ultimately causes Rick to shatter when&nbsp;
he is nearly forced to mutilate his son Carl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.799 --> 00:10:18.167
As Glenn's widow and the mother of his child,&nbsp;
Maggie has not had an easy time with Negan.

00:10:18.298 --> 00:10:19.558
"Glenn was beautiful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.119 --> 00:10:24.979
I'll never love anyone like that again."

00:10:25.579 --> 00:10:30.859
Though Negan's actions are unforgivable, Maggie&nbsp;
knows she's going to have to depend on him going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.859 --> 00:10:36.079
forward, which forces her to accept his attempts&nbsp;
at making amends. Perhaps most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.079 --> 00:10:41.239
the series finale saw Negan finally&nbsp;
apologize after years of wrongdoing. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.239 --> 00:10:44.779
never fully understood what he'd taken&nbsp;
from Maggie when he murdered Glenn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:48.079
but his relationship with Annie&nbsp;
has profoundly changed his outlook.

00:10:48.517 --> 00:10:55.117
"I am so sorry for what I took from you."

00:10:55.459 --> 00:11:00.499
One of the best things about The Walking Dead&nbsp;
has always been its expansive cast. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.499 --> 00:11:04.519
one of the most frustrating aspects&nbsp;
of the show is the impossibility of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.519 --> 00:11:08.539
giving so many top-notch characters&nbsp;
their time in the sun. The finale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.539 --> 00:11:13.579
struggles to wind up dozens of plot threads&nbsp;
and character arcs in a very short time span,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.579 --> 00:11:17.959
and while it mostly succeeds, some of&nbsp;
it's still just a little too brief.

00:11:17.959 --> 00:11:21.979
For example, after a stellar character&nbsp;
arc in the first part of the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.979 --> 00:11:26.839
Yumiko takes a backseat in the finale.&nbsp;
While her romance with Magna is rekindled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.839 --> 00:11:31.339
their story remains severely underplayed, with&nbsp;
only a handful of moments throughout their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.339 --> 00:11:36.739
three seasons on the show. Connie and Kelly had&nbsp;
stellar moments in the 11th season particularly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.739 --> 00:11:41.779
but we don't see much of them here. Father&nbsp;
Gabriel's goodbye to Rosita is heartbreaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.779 --> 00:11:46.219
but far too brief for a relationship that&nbsp;
has lasted multiple seasons and changed both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.219 --> 00:11:51.319
characters in fundamental ways. Elijah makes&nbsp;
it to safety, but we don't know how. Characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.319 --> 00:11:56.359
are what made The Walking Dead great, and we're&nbsp;
left hoping this isn't the end of our favorites.

00:11:57.259 --> 00:12:02.359
In Episode 1 of The Walking Dead, before anyone&nbsp;
knew it would become a cultural milestone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.359 --> 00:12:05.599
we meet a lonely, scared man named Rick Grimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.599 --> 00:12:09.833
who wakes from a coma and is horrified to&nbsp;
see what's become of the world around him.

00:12:10.117 --> 00:12:16.117
"Little girl? I'm a policeman. Little girl?"

00:12:18.079 --> 00:12:21.259
Rick is saved by his ability&nbsp;
to find community with others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.259 --> 00:12:25.339
then nearly lose them again and again&nbsp;
due to hardship, hostile forces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.339 --> 00:12:30.967
or his own ego. At one point, with hope for the&nbsp;
future at an all-time low, he declares that,

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:33.123
"We are the walking dead."

00:12:33.679 --> 00:12:38.539
With the final "One Year Later" sequence&nbsp;
in "Rest in Peace," one of the series' most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.539 --> 00:12:43.819
shocking turns is the promise of a challenging&nbsp;
future, but also an underlying sense of hope.

00:12:43.819 --> 00:12:46.639
"I want to talk about the future. There's a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.639 --> 00:12:50.339
out there to find out about.&nbsp;
And I think it's time we did."

00:12:50.339 --> 00:12:53.839
It's wild to watch a series once&nbsp;
mired in its own bleak outlook&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:58.498
morph into something optimistic, but that's&nbsp;
exactly where the series finale leaves us.

